# Portfolio Dashboard — Project Role

Admin CMS for managing Hassan Ali's portfolio website content. Built on Minimal UI Kit (MUI + Vite), customized for CRUD over a remote REST API.

## Tech Stack

- **Frontend**: React 19, TypeScript, Vite 6 (port `3039`), MUI 7, Emotion
- **State**: Redux Toolkit (`createSlice`, `createAsyncThunk`)
- **Routing**: React Router 7 (lazy-loaded pages, `DashboardLayout`)
- **Forms**: React Hook Form + Zod (`@hookform/resolvers/zod`)
- **HTTP**: Axios via `src/config/api.config.ts` → base URL `https://protfilio-backend.vercel.app/api`
- **Path alias**: `src/` (configured in `vite.config.ts` and `tsconfig.json`)

## Folder Structure

```
src/
├── pages/           # Thin route wrappers (set title, render section)
├── sections/        # Feature UI and business logic
├── stores/
│   ├── index.ts     # configureStore + RootState/AppDispatch types
│   └── slices/      # One slice per domain (async thunks + reducers)
├── schemas/         # Zod schemas + inferred TypeScript types
├── components/      # Shared UI (FormLayouts, TableResued, ModelResuble, etc.)
├── layouts/         # DashboardLayout, AuthLayout, nav configs
├── routes/          # Route definitions (sections.tsx), hooks, error boundary
├── theme/           # MUI theme (palette, typography, shadows)
├── context/         # ToastProvider
├── hooks/           # Custom hooks (useToast)
└── config/          # api.config.ts
```

## Redux Domains

| Slice key   | File                  | Domain                          |
|-------------|-----------------------|---------------------------------|
| `section`   | slices/sections.ts    | Section visibility toggles      |
| `global`    | slices/global.ts      | Global settings (contact, CV)   |
| `social`    | slices/social.ts      | Social media links              |
| `profile`   | slices/profile.ts     | Profile/hero content            |
| `portfolio` | slices/portfolio.ts   | Portfolio projects (CRUD)       |
| `skills`    | slices/skills.ts      | Skills section                  |
| `experience`| slices/experience.ts  | Work experience                 |

Slice pattern: `{ loading, data, error }` initial state → `createAsyncThunk` API calls → `extraReducers` for pending/fulfilled/rejected.

## Routes & Navigation

Routes live in `src/routes/sections.tsx`. Nav items in `src/layouts/nav-config-dashboard.tsx`. When adding a page, update **both** files.

| Path                      | Page / Section              |
|---------------------------|-----------------------------|
| `/`                       | Dashboard (analytics)       |
| `/sections`               | Section visibility          |
| `/global`                 | Global settings + social    |
| `/profile-content`        | Profile content             |
| `/about-section`          | About section               |
| `/work-section`           | Work process section        |
| `/portfolio-section`      | Portfolio list              |
| `/portfolio-section/:id`  | Portfolio details           |
| `/portfolio-section/create` | Portfolio create          |
| `/contact-section`        | Contact section             |
| `/skills-section`         | Skills section              |
| `/experience`             | Experience section          |

## Reusable Patterns

- **Forms**: `FormLayouts<T>` + Zod schema + `FormLayoutItem[]` layout config
- **Tables**: `ReusableTable<T>` with columns, actions (edit/toggle/delete), create button
- **Modals**: `ModelReusable` wrapping forms or confirm dialogs
- **Toasts**: `useToast()` → `showSuccess`, `showError`, etc.
- **Page shell**: Wrap content in `<DashboardContent maxWidth="xl">`
- **Bilingual fields**: `{ ar: string; en: string }` (`LocalizedText`) for portfolio items

## Adding a New Section (Checklist)

1. Create Zod schema in `src/schemas/`
2. Create Redux slice in `src/stores/slices/`, register in `src/stores/index.ts`
3. Build UI in `src/sections/<name>/index.tsx`
4. Add thin page in `src/pages/`
5. Lazy-import page + add route in `src/routes/sections.tsx`
6. Add nav entry in `src/layouts/nav-config-dashboard.tsx`

## Conventions

- Match existing slice/thunk naming: `GetAllX`, `CreateX`, `UpdateX`, `DeleteX`, `ChangeVisiablillity`
- API responses use `{ success, data }` shape; check `res.payload.success` after dispatch
- Use MUI `sx` prop for styling; theme vars via `minimal-shared/utils`
- Do **not** rename existing typos unless explicitly asked: `portilioSection`, `porfolitoSection`, `ModelResuble`, `TableResued`, `workPorgressSection`
- Keep pages thin; put logic in sections and Redux slices
- Minimize scope — one focused change per task

